            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-09-02T15:06:11.918+0000",
          "updated": "2009-09-02T15:06:11.918+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12434567/comment/12750477",
          "id": "12750477",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "I searched just now, but couldn't find, an email thread I recall on java-dev between Doug Cutting and the RM at that point (several years ago) about modifying past releases' CHANGES.txt entries.  Doug's position, articulated both in that thread (and elsewhere, IIRC), was that people depend on being able to do a diff between CHANGES.txt versions, so once a release was cut, the release notes should never change thereafter.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
